[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: The systems a reader can switch on and off

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @repo

[NARRATIVE]
UID: NAR-CANON-SYSTEMS
TITLE: The systems a reader can switch on and off
DEPTH: interface-settled
AUTHORED_BY: llm
WIDGET: table
PLACE: card
TAGS: systems
STATEMENT: >>>
| system | sources | switch | meaning |
| model | docs/spec/ | always | the shared model every other system cites: the node types, the state ladders and the ruled words |
| adoption | docs/plans/canon-adoption/ | optional | lifting the rest of the repository into the canon: what dissolves, what becomes evidence |
| architecture | packages/ | optional | settled design co-located with the package it describes |
| beads | docs/plans/beads-migration/ | optional | the working store the canon will hand execution to |
| core | docs/plans/strictdoc-tooling/ | optional | the canon's own tooling: the grammar, the scribe, the checks and the hooks |
| whiteboard | docs/plans/whiteboard-view/ | optional | the view system that renders the canon for a person to read |
<<<
PARENT_FP: >>>
DEC-SYSTEM-IS-A-TYPE-SET:0000000
<<<
